WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.710
A UK supermarket in winter.

2
00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:07.750
The labels read Spain, South
Africa, Costa Rica, Kenya.

3
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.870
Outside, farms stretch across the country.

4
00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:14.950
Yet the UK produces only
about 60 per cent of its food.

5
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.050
It imports about 40.

6
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.710
Food isn't alone.

7
00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:23.550
In 2024, the UK produced only
about half the gas it used.

8
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.150
So why does so much of
Britain's food come from abroad?

9
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.460
Is imported food just cheaper?

10
00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:33.510
In this mission, you'll find out how
much of its own food the UK grows,

11
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:36.470
and map where the rest comes from.

12
00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:38.550
Then you'll weigh food's carbon footprint,

13
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.170
and the rise of big agribusiness farms.

14
00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:46.840
Your mission: explain why so much
of Britain's food comes from abroad.
